d3483989953ae3cccd773aea5ea04cb0c7198531:docs/UpdatingMajorVersionAndTFM.md:46:  * Exceptions to this are [eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.csproj](/eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.csproj) and [eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.tasks](/eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.tasks). These build without the workarounds from [eng/tools/GenerateFiles/Directory.Build.targets.in](/eng/tools/GenerateFiles/Directory.Build.targets.in), and need to be kept at the previous TFM until we get an SDK containing a runtime with the new TFM. Generally this means we have to hard-code the previous TFM for these files, rather than using `DefaultNetCoreTargetFramework`.
d3483989953ae3cccd773aea5ea04cb0c7198531:docs/UpdatingMajorVersionAndTFM.md:69:Typically we update the SDK we use in `main` every Monday. Once we have one that contains `Microsoft.Netcore.App` entries with the new TFM, we can update [eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.csproj](/eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.csproj) and [eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.tasks](/eng/tools/RepoTasks/RepoTasks.tasks) to use `DefaultNetCoreTargetFramework` again rather than hard-coding the previous TFM.
